{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1794172944,"nonce":"TiuH0CoVrMWNqKne+TmqEWYWQaE=","target":"ccb2c4f7a8a6a946c9b11f26313b4500e47cea765ccd0dfb593fa3cfba1468d9","message":"## Context\n`/roadmap-done` closes open bugs whose `Refs:` trailer is already on the base branch. The app should do the same per repo, natively.\n\n## Files\n- `src/done.rs` — new, in lib: base resolution + candidates\n- `src/ui/screen.rs` — \"Roadmap Done\" action on Repositories page + review sheet\n\n## Approach\n- Port `resolve_base` (`../skillforge/plugins/roadmap/skills/gb/scripts/gb:139-152`): `.claude/roadmap.json` `baseBranch` → `origin/HEAD` → first of `main trunk master develop` that exists locally or on origin.\n- Port `cmd_merged` (`gb:154-183`) as an async fn: `git log \u003cbase\u003e [origin/\u003cbase\u003e] --grep='^Refs: ' --format='%h%x1f%s%x1f%(trailers:key=Refs,valueonly,separator=%x20)'`; no fetch; a non-epic open bug is a candidate when a trailer id (≥7 chars, lowercased) prefixes its full id; keep matching commits as evidence. Uses already-loaded issues, no extra git-bug call.\n- Epic qualifies only when every child is closed or selected for closing now; close it after its children; it stays open if any child close fails (README `/roadmap-done` row).\n- Sheet opens immediately with a loading state while candidates compute; one checkbox row per candidate with its commits, all/none, Close; results ticked per row as each L7 `close` completes.\n\n## Depends on\nL7 — `close`\n\n## Out of scope\n- Fetching remotes, PR mode.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Temp-repo tests: a commit with `Refs: \u003cprefix\u003e` makes that open bug a candidate; one without the trailer doesn't; base resolution honors `baseBranch` before trunk names\n- Unit test: epic qualifies only when all children are closed or selected\n- All three gates pass","files":null}]}